{"name":"Orchestra of Red","hex":"#ae230e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"orchestra","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large group of musicians who play together on various instruments, usually including some from strings, woodwind, brass and/or percussion; the instruments played by such a group.","A semicircular space in front of the stage used by the chorus in Ancient Greek and Hellenistic theatres."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orchestra"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Orchestra","blocks":[{"text":"An orchestra is a large instrumental ensemble typical of classical music or jazz, which combines instruments from different families. There are typically four main sections of instruments:"},{"items":["The string section, including the violin, viola, cello, and double bass","The woodwind section, including the flute, oboe, clarinet, and bassoon, and sometimes piccolo, cor anglais, bass clarinet, contrabassoon, and saxophone","The brass section, including the French horn, trumpet, trombone, and tuba, and sometimes cornet and euphonium","The percussion section, including the timpani, snare drum, bass drum, cymbals, triangle, tambourine, tam-tam and mallet percussion instruments"]}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/National_Chamber_Orchestra_of_Armenia.jpg/330px-National_Chamber_Orchestra_of_Armenia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orchestra","wikidata":"Q42998"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Cincinnati_Symphony_Orchestra_Wikivoyage_FTT.jpg/500px-Cincinnati_Symphony_Orchestra_Wikivoyage_FTT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Cincinnati_Symphony_Orchestra_Wikivoyage_FTT.jpg/1280px-Cincinnati_Symphony_Orchestra_Wikivoyage_FTT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Cincinnati_Symphony_Orchestra_Wikivoyage_FTT.jpg/500px-Cincinnati_Symphony_Orchestra_Wikivoyage_FTT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cincinnati Symphony Orchestra","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACincinnati_Symphony_Orchestra_Wikivoyage_FTT.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Philadelphia_Orchestra_at_American_premiere_of_Mahler%27s_8th_Symphony_%281916%29.jpg/500px-Philadelphia_Orchestra_at_American_premiere_of_Mahler%27s_8th_Symphony_%281916%29.jpg?utm_s